  "_commit": {
    "id": "4232eaf043694b8b8e2bfe1095f03185be39a8af",
    "author": "Sean Davis <seandavi@gmail.com>",
    "committer": "GitHub <noreply@github.com>",
    "message": "Install methylumi into the real library before building the pkgdown site (#52)\n\npkgdown::build_site(install = TRUE) installs the package into a temporary\nlibrary that exists only on the calling R process's .libPaths(). The articles\nare .qmd, so pkgdown renders them by shelling out to the Quarto CLI, which\nstarts a fresh R session per file -- and that session inherits none of the\ntemporary library. library(methylumi) in the vignettes therefore resolved\nagainst the stale methylumi already in the container's site-library, and the\nbuild died with the long-fixed defunct import from #28:\n\n  ! package or namespace load failed for 'methylumi':\n   object 'parallel' is not exported by 'namespace:lattice'\n  Quitting from methylumi.qmd:83-93 [load]\n\nbuild_site() renders articles with quiet = TRUE, which is why the log showed\nonly 'Error returned by quarto CLI'.\n\nInstall into site-library ourselves and pass install = FALSE, so the child\nQuarto sessions see the package being documented.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
    "time": 1786725194
  },
